WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.420
Fast ejecta catch slower material around the star.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:06.380
At the shock, some organized bulk motion becomes

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:09.360
random thermal motion. The heated plasma can emit

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.120
X rays, while other regions produce optical emission

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.640
lines. The extended remnant is gas on a

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.320
much larger scale than its central compact star.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.360
A Type Two supernova spectrum contains hydrogen lines.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:24.600
Type One lacks those lines. That spectral distinction

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.980
does not uniquely identify the explosion mechanism. A

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.760
massive star can lose its hydrogen envelope before

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.560
collapse, producing a hydrogen poor event in the

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:35.500
Type One b or One c grouping.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:39.090
For the same luminosity, moving ten times farther

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:42.370
away reduces received flux to a hundredth. That

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:45.610
comparison alone does not calculate biological damage. In

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:49.710
the lecture’s atmospheric pathway, energetic radiation reduces ozone,

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:52.690
allowing more solar ultraviolet to reach the surface.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:56.490
Example distances are not sharp universal danger boundaries.
